Something is buggy with resize when resizing to very small image.

If layer is created while painting is in process, result of painting will end up in new layer rather than in which
operation started. That's why reconsider if operations should be executed based on current choose layer index.

When creating a layer, LayerPanel sends that layer is created and index is changed. So core sends two times
curr_idx changed.

Check current_idx between LayerManager and CoreToolManager.

Reconsider if CoreToolManager should send whole layer, not just idx.
